{"duration_api_ms":135727,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"ef7ec260-0ae6-406b-9021-a7922ed1b5d7","total_cost_usd":0.3916995999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":16,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19595,"cache_read_input_tokens":175603,"output_tokens":12927,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":6605},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":19595},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":16,"outputTokens":12927,"cacheReadInputTokens":175603,"cacheCreationInputTokens":19595,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.3916995999999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":6605,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":8,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"A prudent agent exists at modal depth 1, and `check.py` confirms it:\n\n**FORMULA: `(B(a)|B(~a))->B(F)`**, **DEPTH: 1**\n\nIn words, the agent cooperates iff PA can't prove which way the opponent plays against it (or PA is inconsistent).\n\n| opponent | agent's action | opponent's action |\n|---|---|---|\n| CooperateBot | D | C |\n| DefectBot | D | D |\n| FairBot | C | D |\n| itself | C | C |\n\nFairBot defects against it. That doesn't break the definition, which only asks what the agent itself does, but it is a real limitation (see below).\n\n- **Q2 (nothing smaller):** a depth-0 formula with every atom boxed can contain no atoms, so it is just ⊤ or ⊥. ⊤ cooperates with CooperateBot and ⊥ defects against FairBot, so neither is prudent. The minimum depth is therefore 1.\n- **Q3 (all depth-1 prudent agents):**\n  - At depth 1, an agent's move at a world depends only on the set of (a, c, d) value triples seen at earlier worlds. Any function of that set can be written as a depth-1 formula.\n  - Tracing play against the four opponents shows that being prudent comes down to fixed values on exactly six sets. This is a full characterization, and it gives a checker-independent proof that the formula above works.\n  - It also shows that no depth-1 prudent agent can get FairBot to cooperate back. That needs depth 2, e.g. `B(a) & B(~B(F) -> ~d)`, which `check.py` also confirms as prudent.\n  - The six-set rule agreed with `check.py` on all 20,000 random depth-1 formulas I tried.\n- **Smallest size** (counting syntax-tree nodes): an exhaustive search found the minimum depth-1 prudent agent has 9 nodes with constants allowed (the formula above), or 12 without them, e.g. `(B(a)|B(~a))->B(~(a->a))`. That fits the problem's evidence, which only enumerated formulas of up to 7 symbols with no constants. I did not check whether a smaller agent exists at depth 2 or more.\n\nI've written `/work/SUBMIT`.\n\nFiles are in `/work`:\n- answer.md\n- search1.py\n- search1_noconst.py\n- verify1.py","ttft_ms":2178,"type":"result","duration_ms":155524,"uuid":"cf6bb762-8db0-4c84-a901-b72dae25fe81","ttft_stream_ms":1905,"time_to_request_ms":66,"first_content_frame_ms":1905,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
